---
/**
 * The hero — the walk, then the frame.
 *
 * Replaces RtsHero's three movements (the proof landing, the locked door, the
 * roll to the title card). Dion, 17 Sep 2026: keep the scroll through the
 * house, lose the door and the turn — "combine the parallax scroll with the
 * second half". Built first on the harrison-saito-morel template
 * (FrameHero.astro there); this is the same hero in this site's styles.
 *
 * Scroll scrubs the Return to Self film 0 → 15.0 s: the painted room, the
 * doors opening, the four-door room, the dolly to the alcove. A straight line
 * the whole way, no gate. It stops on the alcove frame, where the sharp still
 * dissolves in and the page arrives underneath. If the film cannot load — or
 * before it has — the still holds the screen and pushes in on scroll instead,
 * so the page is never blank and never stuck.
 *
 * The beat (Dion, 18 Sep 2026). Where the door and its VSL card used to be —
 * the four-door room with every door shut, frame 252 (8.42 s) — the walk
 * pauses and "Who this is for" comes up over the doors. It is a pause, not a
 * gate: the runway holds that frame for a stretch (--run-pause), so the film does
 * not move while the panel is up, and a scroll arriving from above is caught
 * there — snapped to the panel and held until the input goes quiet (LOCK_MS /
 * QUIET_MS, never past MAX_LOCK_MS) so a flick or a trackpad's inertia cannot
 * blow past it — then handed straight back. Scrolling on walks through; "Keep
 * walking" does the same. Nothing waits for a tap, and scrolling up is never
 * stopped. The capture-phase wheel/touchmove block is RtsHero's, not
 * lenis.stop(): .lenis-stopped puts overflow:hidden on <html>, which detaches
 * the sticky frame.
 *
 * One custom property, --p (0 at the top, 1 at the alcove), drives the copy,
 * the scrim and the rail; --beat (0–1) drives the panel. The runway is three
 * lengths in CSS (--run-in / --run-pause / --run-out, in vh) that the script reads
 * back, so the film time for a scroll position is piecewise: 0 → 8.42 s over
 * run-in, held over run-pause, 8.42 → 15.0 s over run-out. Seeks are eased with one in
 * flight and three ways to settle, and the iOS unlock is a muted play()
 * paused the moment it resolves (see RtsHero, kept in the tree).
 *
 * The arrival (Dion, 18 Sep 2026). The walk ends on the alcove and holds there
 * for one more stretch (--run-meet) while the room darkens and the page's real
 * hero builds over it, dannymorel.com's layout made our own: the brand at the
 * top, his photograph in the middle with its edges dissolved into the dark,
 * words on the left and words on the right — so arriving reads as the top of a
 * page rather than the end of a film. The photograph is 23-DSC08883 from the
 * 26 Aug shoot (REEL COVER folder, Dion's pick): lit by one small flame at
 * chest height, shoji glowing behind, the bottom two-fifths near-black, which
 * is where the columns sit. The pieces arrive one after another off --meet
 * (photo, then brand, then left, then right). On a phone the photograph is the
 * whole screen — it is 9:16 already — and the words stack at its foot. The
 * words are the template's hero copy (morel.ts HERO) until Dion's own land.
 * Above them, the Japanese (Dion, 18 Sep, "more high end"): a great 和 — wa,
 * harmony — behind his mark, and two vertical columns, 守破離 (the three
 * phases) and 調和 (chōwa, harmony), each moving at its own rate through the
 * arrival (--mp) so they come apart into depth. Set in Yuji Syuku, a brush
 * mincho, self-hosted as a five-glyph subset (fonts/yuji-syuku-kanji-v1.woff2,
 * 4 KB) so every phone draws the same strokes. On desktop the photograph is
 * held at 118% so his face sits just above the middle; on a phone the words
 * sit in three frosted boxes spread down the frame — the quote top right,
 * the headline below his face, the buttons at the foot — rather than one
 * stack at the bottom.
 * (It replaced a seated cut-out of frame 47 the same day; that is in git at
 * 2fe1f93.)
 *
 * The way in (Dion, 18 Sep, "the picture is too dark… start vignetting"). The
 * film runs at a screen brightness of 110–125 to the alcove and the
 * photograph sits near 58, and the arrival used to cover that in one step (a
 * 29-point drop in the last quarter second of film, then a bump as the photo
 * faded in). Now the room closes in from the moment the alcove comes into
 * view (V_FROM, 11.0 s): a vignette from the edges and a dim over the whole,
 * one value, --vig, which runs six tenths of its course over the rest of the
 * walk and the rest over the first 40% of the arrival, and the photograph
 * comes up into the dark as it finishes. One slope, no step.
 *
 * Sooner (Dion, 18 Sep: "they walk into the door and boom — there's a few
 * scrolls missing in between that should be taken out"). The arrival no
 * longer waits for the film to reach the alcove: it starts at the doorway,
 * T_DOOR (10.8 s, once the doors have slid open and the camera passes
 * through), the letters first — the 和 and the two columns — then the
 * photograph, then the words, while the last of the walk plays on under them,
 * dark. The walk out is 80vh (was 140) and the arrival 55vh (was 140): from
 * the end of the pause to a built hero is one screen, not 2.3, and the hold
 * after it is about a third of a screen before the page moves on.
 *
 * The panel is Morel markup (morel.css) inside a bare `.mo` wrapper, scaled
 * to fit whatever height is left between the nav and the consent bar. What it
 * says is a badge set (src/data/badges.ts, Dion 18 Sep): the `set` prop picks
 * one — the home page runs `core` ("our version"), each /lp/<id> landing page
 * runs its own — and the set id goes into sessionStorage so the lead form can
 * tag the enquiry with it. The protectors set's cards are buttons: the pick is
 * tracked and carried to the form too. Without script or with reduced motion
 * the panel never shows, and MorelHome renders the control block instead.
 *
 * The first screen (Dion, 18 Sep): the landing copy is centred, and nothing
 * moves until the visitor does — the film is not played on load (it used to
 * be, for the iOS unlock), the first frame holds as a still, and the unlock
 * happens on the first scroll or touch. Before, a phone showed the alcove
 * still until the film armed and then cut to the first room, which read as a
 * video playing in the background.
 *
 * The call to action sells without selling. (It read "Let me walk with you"
 * for a day; Dion, 19 Sep: too close to the reference. Now "Start the
 * conversation", and only once he has arrived — the first screen and the
 * panel carry no booking button, because it broke the sequence: land, walk
 * in, choose, "Learn more". That button is the only way past the doors; a
 * pick enables it, and walking back up shuts the gate again.)
 *
 * The gate (Dion, 18 Sep, later: "we can't allow the user to scroll past that
 * door… lock until the user selects an option"). The pause is now a gate. The
 * catch lands the scroll on the panel as before, but the hold no longer times
 * out: every card is a button, and the walk goes on once one is tapped (any
 * number; the protectors set takes one). The picks ride to the lead form
 * (fy_pick, comma separated -> GHL tags fy-pick-<card>), the open gate is
 * remembered for the session, and a scroll that meets it nudges the
 * instruction. Up is always free; so is anything plainly deliberate — a link
 * to a section further down, keyboard focus moving past the hero, a page that
 * opens already below the doors. The panel itself went squarer the same day:
 * centred head broken where the colour breaks, six near-square tiles.
 *
 * The title (same day): "Son of a" / "Karate Grand Master", broken at the
 * colour, and the gold line is gold leaf with ink smoke drifting through it
 * (/img/gold-smoke-v1.webp, a seamless alpha tile made by a script — spectral
 * noise, warped, thresholded; two copies at different sizes and speeds).
 *
 * Assets (/video and /img ship with a one-year immutable cache, so a changed
 * file needs a new name):
 *   /video/rts-hero-v4.mp4, -m.mp4    — short-GOP H.264, 720p, 4.6 / 3.0 MB
 *   /img/rts-hero-poster-v3.webp      — the first frame
 *   /img/rts-still-v1-{768…2560}.webp — the 15.0 s frame, upscaled 2x
 */
import { srcset, src } from '../lib/images';
import { HERO as ARRIVE } from '../data/morel';
import { setById, BADGE_SETS } from '../data/badges';
import { forYouIcon } from '../lib/morel-icons';
import '../styles/avant.css';
import '../styles/morel.css';
import '../styles/morel-overrides.css';

const STILL = 'rts-still-v1';

interface Props {
  /** Which "Who This Is For" badge set the pause shows (src/data/badges.ts). */
  set?: string;
}
const SET = setById(Astro.props.set);
const picks = SET.id === 'protectors';

/* The hallway (Dion, 20 Sep): on the walk from the first screen to the doors,
   badges come up left and right of the corridor and pass him, so that by the
   time the panel asks "who is this for" he has already walked through the
   answers. They are lines from the OTHER badge sets — never the six the panel
   is about to show — one from each set in turn, and never a line marked `new`
   (those are ours, not yet Harrison's, and live in one place only). */
const HALL_N = 8;
/* Lines Dion has pulled from the page (19 Sep) do not come back through the hall. */
const HALL_SKIP = new Set(['and you call it normal.']);
const own = new Set(SET.badges.map((b) => b.text + b.emphasis));
const seen = new Set<string>();
const HALL: { icon: string; text: string; emphasis: string }[] = [];
for (let round = 0; round < 6 && HALL.length < HALL_N; round++) {
  for (const set of BADGE_SETS) {
    if (set.id === SET.id || HALL.length >= HALL_N) continue;
    const b = set.badges[round];
    if (!b || b.kind === 'new' || HALL_SKIP.has(b.emphasis)) continue;
    const key = b.text + b.emphasis;
    if (own.has(key) || seen.has(key) || seen.has(b.icon)) continue;
    seen.add(key); seen.add(b.icon);
    HALL.push({ icon: b.icon, text: b.text, emphasis: b.emphasis });
  }
}
/* Where each one stands: its height in the frame, and when it is level with
   him, as a fraction of the walk to the doors (0.34 = the title has just
   gone, 0.80 = clear before the panel comes up). */
const HALL_Y = [22, 42, 58, 20, 30, 60, 62, 34];   /* same-side neighbours alternate high and low */
const hallAt = (i: number) => (0.34 + (i * 0.46) / (HALL_N - 1)).toFixed(3);
---

<section class="hero" id="hero" data-frame-hero data-fy={SET.id} data-section="hero" aria-label="Harrison Saito — Return to Self">
  <div class="hero__frame">
    <img class="hero__poster" src="/img/rts-hero-poster-v3.webp" alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="1280" height="720" fetchpriority="high" decoding="sync" />
    <video class="hero__film" muted playsinline preload="metadata"
           aria-label="A slow walk through a traditional Japanese house, arriving at an alcove with a hanging scroll."></video>
    <img
      class="hero__plate"
      src={src(STILL)}
      srcset={srcset(STILL) || undefined}
      sizes="100vw"
      alt="A traditional Japanese room, its sliding doors open onto an alcove with a hanging scroll"
      width="1920"
      height="1080"
      loading="eager"
      decoding="async"
    />
    <div class="hero__scrim" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="hero__veil" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="hero__vignette" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    {/* The hallway's badges: decoration for the walk, read out nowhere — the
        panel that follows is where the lines are said. */}
    <div class="hall" aria-hidden="true">
      {HALL.map((c, i) => (
        <p class={`hall__chip hall__chip--${i % 2 ? 'r' : 'l'}`} style={`--f:${hallAt(i)};--y:${HALL_Y[i % HALL_Y.length]}%`}>
          <Fragment set:html={forYouIcon(c.icon)} />
          <span>{c.text} <strong>{c.emphasis}</strong></span>
        </p>
      ))}
    </div>

    <div class="hero__copy">
      <p class="hero__eyebrow"><span>Harrison Saito · Coaching</span><i aria-hidden="true"> · </i><span>Chatswood, Sydney</span></p>
      <h1 class="hero__title">You don’t have to react<br /><mark>to everything you feel.</mark></h1>
      <p class="hero__sub">17+ Years Karate | Coach | Buddhist</p>
      {/* A row of four client interviews stood here for a day (20-21 Sep). Dion took
          it off: too much too soon, and four men in front of the same curtain read as
          staged. The component and the cut list are kept (InterviewRow.astro,
          data/interviews.ts); the clips are out of /public until they have a place. */}
      {/* One way on (Dion, 19 Sep): no booking button up here — it broke the
          sequence (land, walk in, choose, learn more). The booking asks come
          once he has arrived. */}
      <p class="hero__ctas">
        <a class="hero__more" href="#for-you" data-beat-go data-track="cta_click" data-track-label="Hero — Start here" data-track-section="hero">Start here ↓</a>
      </p>
    </div>

    {/* The beat: "Who this is for", over the four shut doors. */}
    <div class="beat mo mo--bare" data-beat aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="beat__panel" role="region" aria-label="Who This Is For">
        <header class="beat__head">
          <p class="eyebrow beat__eyebrow">Who This Is For</p>
          <h2 class="beat__title" set:html={SET.title} />
          <p class="beat__lede">{SET.lede}</p>
        </header>
        {/* Every card is a button (Dion, 18 Sep): the walk does not go on
            until one is tapped. Any number can be — except the protectors
            set, which asks for the one. */}
        <div class="fy__grid beat__grid" data-stagger data-picks={picks ? 'one' : 'many'} role="group" aria-label={picks ? 'Tap the one that runs you' : 'Tap what is true for you'}>
          {SET.badges.map((c, i) => (
            <button type="button" class="fy__card reveal beat__card" style={`--k:${i}`} data-pick={c.tag ?? c.icon} aria-pressed="false" data-track="fy_pick" data-track-label={c.tag ?? c.icon} data-track-section="hero-beat">
              <Fragment set:html={forYouIcon(c.icon)} />
              <p>{c.tag && <span class="beat__tag">{c.tag}</span>}{c.text} <strong>{c.emphasis}</strong></p>
            </button>
          ))}
        </div>
        <p class="beat__foot">
          <button class="beat__on" type="button" data-beat-on aria-disabled="true" data-track="cta_click" data-track-label={`Beat (${SET.id}) — Learn more`} data-track-section="hero-beat" data-closed={picks ? 'Tap the one that runs you' : 'Tap what’s true for you'} data-open="Learn more ↓">{picks ? 'Tap the one that runs you' : 'Tap what’s true for you'}</button>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    {/* The arrival: the page's hero, built over the room the walk ends in. */}
    <div class="arrive" data-meet>
      <img
        class="arrive__photo"
        src="/img/harrison-arrival-v1.webp"
        srcset="/img/harrison-arrival-v1-640.webp 640w, /img/harrison-arrival-v1-900.webp 900w, /img/harrison-arrival-v1-1152.webp 1152w"
        sizes="(max-width: 760px) 100vw, (max-aspect-ratio: 4/5) 100vw, 52vh"
        alt="Harrison Saito in the dojo at night, lit by a single small flame, shoji glowing behind him"
        width="1152"
        height="2048"
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
      <div class="arrive__shade" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      {/* The match he is holding, alive: light laid over the photograph's own
          flame (script places it; see "the flame" in the styles). */}
      <div class="arrive__flame" data-flame aria-hidden="true">
        <i class="flame__face"></i>
        <i class="flame__halo"></i>
        <i class="flame__core"><b></b></i>
      </div>

      {/* The Japanese: set once, each on its own parallax rate. */}
      <p class="arrive__kanji" lang="ja" aria-hidden="true">和</p>
      <p class="arrive__vert arrive__vert--l" lang="ja" aria-hidden="true"><span>守破離</span><small>shu · ha · ri</small></p>
      <p class="arrive__vert arrive__vert--r" lang="ja" aria-hidden="true"><span>調和</span><small>chōwa · harmony</small></p>

      <p class="arrive__brand">
        <img src="/img/logo-light-512.webp" alt="" width="56" height="56" loading="lazy" />
        <span>Harrison Saito</span>
      </p>

      <div class="arrive__left">
        <div class="arrive__words">
          <p class="arrive__title" set:html={ARRIVE.titleLines.join('<br />')} />
          <p class="arrive__accent" set:html={ARRIVE.accent} />
        </div>
        <p class="arrive__ctas">
          <a class="hero__btn" href={ARRIVE.cta.href} data-track="cta_click" data-track-label="Arrival — Book a discovery chat" data-track-section="hero-arrival"><span class="cta-long">{ARRIVE.cta.label}</span><span class="cta-short">Talk with me</span></a>
          <a class="hero__more" href="/mens-coaching" data-track="cta_click" data-track-label="Arrival — See the programme" data-track-section="hero-arrival">See the program →</a>
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="arrive__right">
        <p class="arrive__quote"><em>{ARRIVE.quoteLines[0]}</em><br /><em>{ARRIVE.quoteLines[1]}</em></p>
        <p class="arrive__big"><mark>{ARRIVE.bigLines[0]}<br />{ARRIVE.bigLines[1]}</mark></p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="hero__cue" aria-hidden="true"><span>Scroll to walk in</span><i></i></div>
    {/* The doorway, as a title card (Dion, 22 Sep). After "Learn more" the room
        is empty and nothing says what to do, so: the name on the right, the
        instruction across the foot, and behind both a class of his ghosted
        into the room — other people, before he has met one. All of it is a
        function of --go (1 from the end of the pause to the doorway). */}
    <div class="hero__enter" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="enter__class"></div>
      <p class="enter__mark"><span>Return</span><span>to Self</span></p>
      <p class="enter__go">
        <span>Scroll to enter</span>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 28 40" width="28" height="40" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 6l9 9 9-9" /><path d="M5 17l9 9 9-9" /><path d="M5 28l9 9 9-9" /></svg>
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="hero__rail" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  /* The runway is the walk, in three lengths (vh): up to the shut doors, the
     pause on them, and on to the alcove. Same pace either side of the pause
     (about 21 vh per film second); the script reads these back. */
  .hero {
    --p: 0;
    --film: 0;                 /* 1 once the film is scrubbing; the poster yields to it */
    --run-in: 180;
    --run-pause: 120;
    --run-out: 80;
    --run-meet: 55;
    --font-avant: 'Avant', 'ITC Avant Garde Gothic', 'Century Gothic', 'Jost', sans-serif;
    position: relative;
    height: calc((100 + var(--run-in) + var(--run-pause) + var(--run-out) + var(--run-meet)) * 1vh);
    background: #14100d;
    color: #fcfaf8;
  }

  /* dvh, not svh — sized to the small viewport the frame stops short of the
     screen when Safari's toolbar collapses (RtsHero learned this on 11 Sep). */
  .hero__frame {
    position: sticky;
    top: 0;
    height: 100vh;
    height: 100dvh;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: #14100d;
  }

  /* Three plates on one axis. The doorway of room one and the alcove of room
     two both sit at plate x ≈ 43–44%, so one crop centre carries the whole
     walk on a portrait phone without any panning. */
  .hero__poster,
  .hero__film,
  .hero__plate {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    max-width: none;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: 44% 50%;
  }
  .hero__poster { z-index: 1; opacity: calc(1 - var(--film)); transition: opacity 0.5s ease; }
  .hero__film { z-index: 2; opacity: var(--film); transition: opacity 0.5s ease; }

  /* The still: the frame the walk ends on. While the film runs it fades in
     only over the last stretch (--hold), so the hand-over from the soft video
     frame to the sharp still is a dissolve, not a cut. Without the film it is
     the whole hero and pushes into the alcove on scroll. */
  .hero__plate {
    z-index: 3;
    opacity: var(--hold, 1);
    transform-origin: 44% 47%;
    transform: scale(calc(1 + var(--push, 0) * 0.34));
    will-change: transform, opacity;
  }

  /* For the nav and the copy; once they have gone the walk is lit by the
     room, with a quarter of the grade kept for grounding. */
  .hero__scrim {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 4;
    pointer-events: none;
    opacity: clamp(0.25, calc(1 - var(--p) * 2.2), 1);
    background:
      linear-gradient(to bottom, rgba(20, 16, 13, 0.55) 0%, rgba(20, 16, 13, 0) 30%),
      linear-gradient(to top, rgba(20, 16, 13, 0.84) 0%, rgba(20, 16, 13, 0.4) 30%, rgba(20, 16, 13, 0) 58%);
  }
  /* Dims the room: under the beat's panel while it is up, and on the way into
     the arrival — --vig (which starts in the walk) plus the arrival's own, as
     one sum, so it only ever deepens. Without the film, --veil still carries
     the still's push-in dim. */
  .hero__veil {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 4;
    pointer-events: none;
    background: #14100d;
    opacity: max(calc(var(--veil, 0) * 0.5 * (1 - var(--meet, 0))), calc(var(--beat, 0) * 0.62), calc(var(--vig, 0) * 0.46 + var(--meet, 0) * 0.28));
    transition: opacity 0.35s ease;
  }
  /* The vignette: the room closing in from its edges, centred on the alcove
     (plate x 44%) so the last thing to go dark is where the photograph will
     stand. */
  /* The doorway title card. --go is 1 from the end of the pause to the
     doorway, where the arrival takes over; everything here rides it. */
  .hero__enter {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 6;
    pointer-events: none;
    opacity: var(--go, 0);
    transition: opacity 0.3s ease;
  }
  /* His class, ghosted into the room: a dojo class at half strength, screened
     so it lights the room rather than covering it, with a scrim under the
     type. (Dion asked for a classroom of faces; this is the nearest thing the
     archive holds — see the note to him. Swapping the file is one line.) */
  .enter__class {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background: url('/img/enter-class-w-v1-1440.webp') 50% 45% / cover no-repeat;
    /* Dion asked for 50%. At 50% the class swallowed the room — the doors
       vanished and it read as a photo, not a presence — so it sits at 0.4
       with the scrim below doing the rest. One number if he wants it up. */
    opacity: 0.4;
  }
  .hero__enter::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background:
      radial-gradient(ellipse 38% 26% at 82% 50%, rgba(20, 16, 13, 0.82) 0%, rgba(20, 16, 13, 0.45) 55%, rgba(20, 16, 13, 0) 100%),
      radial-gradient(ellipse 66% 52% at 46% 44%, rgba(20, 16, 13, 0) 0%, rgba(20, 16, 13, 0.4) 62%, rgba(20, 16, 13, 0.72) 100%),
      linear-gradient(to top, rgba(20, 16, 13, 0.94) 0%, rgba(20, 16, 13, 0.7) 18%, rgba(20, 16, 13, 0.2) 38%, rgba(20, 16, 13, 0) 56%),
      linear-gradient(to left, rgba(20, 16, 13, 0.72) 0%, rgba(20, 16, 13, 0) 46%);
  }
  /* The name, down the right-hand side. */
  .enter__mark {
    position: absolute;
    z-index: 1;
    right: clamp(1.2rem, 4vw, 4.5rem);
    top: 50%;
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    justify-items: end;
    gap: 0.02em;
    font-family: var(--font-avant);
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5.2vw, 5rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 0.92;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    text-align: right;
    /* drop-shadow, not text-shadow: the letters are hollow here, and a text
       shadow would show straight through them */
    filter: drop-shadow(0 2px 10px rgba(20, 16, 13, 0.9)) drop-shadow(0 6px 40px rgba(20, 16, 13, 0.75));
    transform: translateY(calc(-50% + (1 - var(--go, 0)) * 26px));
    transition: transform 0.4s ease;
  }
  /* The fill (Dion, 25 Sep: "keyframe the typography so when the user scrolls
     it fills in the silhouette of the text, and if it scrolls up it goes up as
     well"). Each word is drawn as an outline and its colour is a gradient
     clipped to the glyphs, whose hard edge sits at --gofill — the scroll's own
     position through the doorway, so the fill rises as he goes down and drains
     as he goes back up. No animation, no timer: it is the scroll. */
  .enter__mark span {
    --ink: #fff;
    color: transparent;
    -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;
    -webkit-text-stroke: clamp(1px, 0.055em, 2.4px) rgba(252, 250, 248, 0.62);
    background-image: linear-gradient(
      to top,
      var(--ink) calc(var(--gofill, 0) * 118% - 9%),
      rgba(255, 255, 255, 0) calc(var(--gofill, 0) * 118%)
    );
    -webkit-background-clip: text;
    background-clip: text;
  }
  .enter__mark span:last-child { --ink: #f9d79a; -webkit-text-stroke-color: rgba(249, 215, 154, 0.7); }
  /* No scroll to key off: show the words solid rather than hollow. */
  :global(.no-js) .enter__mark span,
  .enter__mark span:where(:not(:defined)) { -webkit-text-fill-color: currentColor; color: var(--ink); }
  /* The instruction, across the foot. */
  .enter__go {
    position: absolute;
    z-index: 1;
    left: 50%;
    bottom: calc(clamp(1.4rem, 6vh, 4rem) + var(--consent-h, 0px));
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    justify-items: center;
    gap: clamp(6px, 1.4vh, 16px);
    color: #ffe7bb;
    font-family: var(--font-avant);
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 4.2vw, 3.4rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    white-space: nowrap;
    text-shadow: 0 2px 10px rgba(20, 16, 13, 0.95), 0 4px 40px rgba(20, 16, 13, 0.8);
    transform: translate(-50%, calc((1 - var(--go, 0)) * 18px));
    transition: transform 0.3s ease;
  }
  .enter__go span { animation: goNudge 1.5s ease-in-out infinite; }
  .enter__go svg { display: block; width: clamp(34px, 3.4vw, 56px); height: auto; overflow: visible; }
  @keyframes goNudge { 0%, 100% { transform: translateY(0); } 40% { transform: translateY(4px); } }
  .enter__go svg path { animation: goDown 1.5s ease-in-out infinite; opacity: 0.2; }
  .enter__go svg path:nth-child(2) { animation-delay: 0.18s; }
  .enter__go svg path:nth-child(3) { animation-delay: 0.36s; }
  @keyframes goDown { 0%, 100% { opacity: 0.2; transform: translateY(-3px); } 40% { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(3px); } }
  /* A phone: the name sits above the instruction, both hard right and low. */
  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    /* a phone holds one thing at a time: the class is a whisper, the name and
       the instruction stack with air between them */
    .enter__class { background-image: url('/img/enter-class-t-v1-720.webp'); background-position: 50% 38%; opacity: 0.3; }
    .enter__mark { right: 0; left: 0; top: auto; bottom: calc(clamp(1.4rem, 6vh, 4rem) + var(--consent-h, 0px) + 6.4rem); justify-items: center; text-align: center; font-size: clamp(2rem, 13vw, 3.2rem); transform: translateY(calc((1 - var(--go, 0)) * 26px)); }
    .enter__go { font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 6vw, 1.8rem); letter-spacing: 0.16em; }
  }

  /* The hallway. Each chip is a function of --p alone: --t runs -1 -> 1 as he
     walks past it (0 = level with him). It comes up small and close to the
     middle of the corridor, as if from further down it, grows and slides out
     towards its wall as he reaches it, and is gone past his shoulder. --pa is
     the scroll fraction at which the doors arrive (set by the script from the
     runway lengths), so the timing holds whatever the runway is. No script
     per frame, nothing to clean up: before the walk and after it every chip
     sits at opacity 0. */
  .hall {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 4;
    overflow: hidden;
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  .hall__chip {
    --span: calc(var(--pa, 0.41) * 0.135);
    --t: calc((var(--p, 0) - var(--pa, 0.41) * var(--f)) / var(--span));
    --a: max(var(--t), calc(var(--t) * -1));
    position: absolute;
    top: var(--y);
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
    max-width: min(24rem, 29vw);
    padding: 12px 18px 11px 14px;
    border-radius: 16px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(242, 194, 117, 0.38);
    background: rgba(20, 16, 13, 0.74);
    box-shadow: 0 18px 50px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.45);
    color: #fcfaf8;
    font-family: var(--font-avant);
    font-size: clamp(0.74rem, 0.62rem + 0.42vw, 1.02rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.18;
    letter-spacing: -0.005em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    text-wrap: balance;
    opacity: clamp(0, calc(1.75 - var(--a) * 1.75), 1);
    will-change: transform, opacity;
  }
  .hall__chip strong { display: block; color: #f2c275; font-weight: 700; }
  .hall__chip :global(.fy__icon) { flex: none; width: 34px; height: 34px; color: #f2c275; }
  .hall__chip--l {
    left: clamp(12px, 5.5vw, 104px);
    transform-origin: 0 50%;
    transform: translate3d(calc(var(--t) * -8vw), calc(var(--t) * -2.5vh), 0) scale(calc(1 + var(--t) * 0.2));
  }
  .hall__chip--r {
    right: clamp(12px, 5.5vw, 104px);
    transform-origin: 100% 50%;
    transform: translate3d(calc(var(--t) * 8vw), calc(var(--t) * -2.5vh), 0) scale(calc(1 + var(--t) * 0.2));
  }
  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .hall__chip { max-width: 45vw; gap: 8px; padding: 9px 11px 8px 9px; border-radius: 13px; font-size: 0.66rem; }
    .hall__chip :global(.fy__icon) { width: 24px; height: 24px; }
    .hall__chip--l { left: 8px; }
    .hall__chip--r { right: 8px; }
  }

  .hero__vignette {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 4;
    pointer-events: none;
    background: radial-gradient(ellipse 72% 68% at 44% 46%, rgba(20, 16, 13, 0) 28%, rgba(20, 16, 13, 0.5) 60%, rgba(20, 16, 13, 0.94) 100%);
    opacity: var(--vig, 0);
  }

  /* Centred on the screen, both ways (Dion, 18 Sep): the title the visitor
     lands on sits in the middle of the room, not in a corner of it. */
  .hero__copy {
    position: absolute;
    z-index: 5;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    /* The middle of what is FREE: between the nav and the consent bar while it
       is up (it is a fifth of a laptop screen), so the row of interviews and
       the way on are never under it. */
    top: calc(50% + 40px - var(--consent-h, 0px) / 2);
    transition: top 0.45s ease;
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-inline: clamp(1.25rem, 5vw, 5.5rem);
    max-width: 80rem;
    display: grid;
    justify-items: center;
    text-align: center;
    gap: clamp(0.75rem, 2vw, 1.5rem);
    font-family: var(--font-avant);
    opacity: clamp(0, calc(1 - var(--p) * 9), 1);
    transform: translateY(calc(-50% + var(--p) * -300px));
    will-change: opacity, transform;
  }
  /* One line where it fits. Where it cannot, it is two lines broken on
     purpose — name and work, then the place — never "Sydney" left alone under
     the rest (Dion, 18 Sep). Each phrase is unbreakable; below 620px the
     second separator goes and the place takes its own line, and the type
     scales so the longer phrase always fits a 320px screen. */
  .hero__eyebrow {
    font-size: clamp(0.66rem, 3.1vw, 0.8rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.22em;
    line-height: 1.7;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #f2c275;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .hero__eyebrow span { white-space: nowrap; }
  .hero__eyebrow i { font-style: normal; }
  @media (max-width: 620px) {
    .hero__eyebrow { letter-spacing: 0.18em; }
    .hero__eyebrow i { display: none; }
    .hero__eyebrow span { display: block; }
  }
  /* Two lines, broken where the colour breaks: "You don't have to react" in
     white, then "to everything you feel." in the smoked gold — the voice
     guide's primary hero line (docs/VOICE.md §3, Dion, 25 Sep). The size
     follows the width (6.2vw: the longer line is 23 characters where "Break
     the habits" was 16) so it fits on one line from a 320px phone up, and
     fills most of the measure while it does; fitHeadings is the net under it.
     (19–25 Sep this was "Break the habits / you never chose."; until 19 Sep
     "Son of a / Karate Grand Master", which now stands in the arrival.) */
  .hero__title {
    font-family: var(--font-avant);
    font-size: clamp(1.35rem, min(6.2vw, 11vh), 4.2rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    line-height: 0.92;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #fcfaf8;
    margin: 0;
    text-wrap: balance;
    text-shadow: 0 2px 30px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35);
  }
  /* Gold leaf with ink in it (Dion, 18 Sep): the gold stays, and a dark mist
     drifts through the letters the way cloud bands cross a gold-leaf screen.
     Two copies of one seamless smoke tile (alpha, the site's ink) over the
     leaf, sized in em so the wisps stay letter-sized at every width, each
     travelling exactly one tile per loop so the loop has no seam. */
  .hero__title mark {
    background:
      url('/img/gold-smoke-v1.webp') 0 0 / 11em 5.5em repeat,
      url('/img/gold-smoke-v1.webp') 6em 3em / 17em 8.5em repeat,
      linear-gradient(100deg, #f9e0a3 0%, #f2c275 20%, #c48c3a 46%, #f3ca80 64%, #daa24f 82%, #a5732a 100%);
    -webkit-background-clip: text;
    background-clip: text;
    -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;
    color: #f2c275;
    animation: goldSmoke 80s linear infinite;
  }
  @keyframes goldSmoke {
    to { background-position: 11em 0, -11em 3em, 0 0; }
  }
  /* Off screen it holds still: nothing repaints under the walk. */
  .hero--away .hero__title mark { animation-play-state: paused; }
  /* Under the title, never larger than it: the title now runs at 6.2vw, so
     on a phone the old 1.6rem floor sat above it. Same size on a desk. */
  .hero__sub {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 0.9rem + 1.6vw, 2.15rem);
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.2;
    margin: 0;
    color: rgba(252, 250, 248, 0.92);
  }

  .hero__ctas {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: clamp(0.75rem, 2vw, 1.5rem) clamp(1rem, 2.5vw, 2rem);
    margin: clamp(0.5rem, 1.5vw, 1rem) 0 0;
  }
  /* The gold pill; the 2px ring shows on hover, drawn under a masked pseudo. */
  .hero__btn {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    display: inline-block;
    border-radius: 100px;
    padding: 0.65rem clamp(1.25rem, 4vw, 3rem) 0.5rem;
    background: linear-gradient(to right, #f2c275 0%, #daa24f 100%);
    color: #14100d;
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 0.94rem + 0.3vw, 1.25rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    line-height: 1.6;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    text-decoration: none;
    text-align: center;
    transition: all 0.3s ease-in-out;
  }
  .hero__btn::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    border-radius: inherit;
    padding: 2px;
    background: linear-gradient(to right, #f2c275 0%, #daa24f 100%);
    -webkit-mask: linear-gradient(#fff 0 0) content-box, linear-gradient(#fff 0 0);
    -webkit-mask-composite: xor;
    mask: linear-gradient(#fff 0 0) content-box, linear-gradient(#fff 0 0);
    mask-composite: exclude;
    pointer-events: none;
    opacity: 0;
    transition: opacity 0.3s ease-in-out;
  }
  .hero__btn:hover { background: #fff; color: #14100d; box-shadow: 0 5px 30px rgba(218, 162, 79, 0.4); }
  .hero__btn:hover::before { opacity: 1; }
  .hero__btn:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid #daa24f; outline-offset: 2px; }
  /* The arrival's button says it in full where there is room, and in the
     nav's three words where the full line would wrap and strand a word. */
  .cta-short { display: none; }
  @media (max-width: 900px) { .cta-long { display: none; } .cta-short { display: inline; } }

  .hero__more {
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.72);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-color: rgba(218, 162, 79, 0.6);
    text-underline-offset: 0.25em;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .hero__more:hover { color: #fcfaf8; text-decoration-color: #daa24f; }

  /* The sign that the frame moves. Goes with the first scroll. */
  .hero__cue {
    position: absolute;
    z-index: 5;
    left: 50%;
    transform: translateX(-50%);
    bottom: calc(clamp(1.4rem, 5vh, 3.2rem) + var(--consent-h, 0px));
    display: grid;
    justify-items: center;
    gap: 0.55rem;
    font-family: var(--font-avant);
    font-size: 0.62rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.26em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    white-space: nowrap;
    color: rgba(252, 250, 248, 0.7);
    opacity: clamp(0, calc(1 - var(--p) * 30), 1);
  }
  .hero__cue i { display: block; width: 1px; height: 52px; background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.18); position: relative; overflow: hidden; }
  .hero__cue i::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: -45%;
    width: 100%;
    height: 45%;
    background: #daa24f;
    animation: hero-cue 2.2s cubic-bezier(0.6, 0, 0.4, 1) infinite;
  }
  @keyframes hero-cue { 0% { top: -45%; } 60%, 100% { top: 100%; } }

  /* How far along the walk is — a hairline at the foot of the frame. */
  .hero__rail { position: absolute; z-index: 5; left: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0; height: 2px; background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12); }
  .hero__rail i { display: block; height: 100%; width: calc(var(--p) * 100%); background: #daa24f; }

  /* ---- the arrival ----------------------------------------------------
     The hero the walk arrives at. Everything is a function of --meet (0–1),
     each piece on its own slice of it so they land one after another:
     photograph 0–.45, brand and kanji .2–.5, left .35–.75, right .5–.9. The
     kanji also ride --mp, the raw progress through the whole arrival, so they
     keep drifting — at three different rates — after the words have landed.
     A piece is only hit-testable once .hero--meet is on (visibility). */
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Kanji Brush';
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-display: swap;
    src: url('/fonts/yuji-syuku-kanji-v1.woff2') format('woff2');
    unicode-range: U+548C, U+5B88, U+7834, U+8ABF, U+96E2;
  }
  .arrive {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 6;
    /* The letters come up first, as the camera goes through the doorway;
       the photograph rises into the room as it goes dark; then the words. */
    --a-brand: clamp(0, calc(var(--meet, 0) / 0.26), 1);
    --a-photo: clamp(0, calc((var(--meet, 0) - 0.14) / 0.36), 1);
    --a-left: clamp(0, calc((var(--meet, 0) - 0.4) / 0.3), 1);
    --a-right: clamp(0, calc((var(--meet, 0) - 0.5) / 0.3), 1);
    --pad-x: clamp(1.25rem, 5vw, 5.5rem);
    --pad-b: calc(clamp(1.8rem, 6vh, 4.5rem) + var(--consent-h, 0px));
    --kanji: 'Kanji Brush', 'Yuji Syuku', 'Yu Mincho', 'Hiragino Mincho ProN', 'Noto Serif JP', serif;
    visibility: hidden;
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  .hero--meet .arrive { visibility: visible; pointer-events: auto; }

  /* The photograph, held at 118% so his face sits just above the middle of
     the screen; its sides dissolve into the darkened room, so it reads as lit
     out of the dark rather than framed. Its top and foot fall off-screen. */
  .arrive__photo {
    position: absolute;
    left: 50%;
    top: -6%;
    height: 118%;
    width: auto;
    max-width: none;
    object-fit: cover;
    opacity: var(--a-photo);
    transform: translateX(-50%) scale(calc(1.06 - var(--a-photo) * 0.06));
    transform-origin: 50% 40%;
    -webkit-mask-image: linear-gradient(to right, transparent 0%, #000 22%, #000 78%, transparent 100%), linear-gradient(to top, transparent 0%, #000 18%);
    -webkit-mask-composite: source-in;
    mask-image: linear-gradient(to right, transparent 0%, #000 22%, #000 78%, transparent 100%), linear-gradient(to top, transparent 0%, #000 18%);
    mask-composite: intersect;
    will-change: opacity, transform;
  }
  .arrive__shade { display: none; }

  /* The flame. In the photograph (1152 x 2048) the match is a blown-out flare
     47.4% across and 56.7% down, ~110px wide, streaked to the right by the
     exposure, with smoke lifting up-right to his jaw. It cannot move — it is
     a still — so light is laid over it and THAT moves: a hot core on the
     flare, a halo round it, and a wash on the cheek it lights. The script
     lays this box exactly over the photograph's own box (it is cropped
     differently on a phone) and drives five numbers from the SCROLL, not the
     clock — brightness, sway x/y, stretch x/y, summed sines of the scroll
     position at unrelated periods — so the flame gutters as he moves and is
     steady when he stops; a breath of idle flicker keeps it alive at rest.
     Screen-blended, so it can only add light. */
  .arrive__flame {
    position: absolute;
    left: var(--fb-x, 0);
    top: var(--fb-y, 0);
    width: var(--fb-w, 0);
    height: var(--fb-h, 0);
    pointer-events: none;
    mix-blend-mode: screen;
    opacity: var(--a-photo);
    transform: scale(calc(1.06 - var(--a-photo) * 0.06));
    transform-origin: 50% 40%;
  }
  .arrive__flame i { position: absolute; left: var(--fl-cx, 47.4%); top: var(--fl-cy, 56.7%); display: block; border-radius: 50%; }
  .flame__core {
    width: calc(var(--fl-size, 60px) * 1.5);
    height: calc(var(--fl-size, 60px) * 0.95);
    margin: calc(var(--fl-size, 60px) * -0.5) 0 0 calc(var(--fl-size, 60px) * -0.55);
    transform: translate(calc(var(--fl-x, 0) * 1px), calc(var(--fl-y, 0) * 1px)) scale(var(--fl-kx, 1), var(--fl-ky, 1));
    transform-origin: 35% 60%;
    opacity: var(--fl-i, 0.9);
  }
  .flame__core b {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    border-radius: 50%;
    /* closest-side: every light here must reach nothing AT its own edge, or the
       edge shows as a disc on the photograph */
    background: radial-gradient(ellipse closest-side at 50% 50%, rgba(255, 247, 224, 0.95) 0%, rgba(255, 214, 140, 0.75) 30%, rgba(255, 160, 60, 0.38) 60%, rgba(255, 120, 30, 0) 100%);
    animation: flameIdle 2.3s ease-in-out infinite;
  }
  .flame__halo {
    width: calc(var(--fl-size, 60px) * 7);
    height: calc(var(--fl-size, 60px) * 6);
    margin: calc(var(--fl-size, 60px) * -3) 0 0 calc(var(--fl-size, 60px) * -3.4);
    background: radial-gradient(ellipse closest-side at 50% 50%, rgba(255, 170, 70, 0.34) 0%, rgba(255, 140, 50, 0.14) 45%, rgba(255, 120, 40, 0.04) 78%, rgba(255, 120, 40, 0) 100%);
    opacity: calc(var(--fl-i, 0.9) * 0.95);
    transform: translate(calc(var(--fl-x, 0) * 0.5px), calc(var(--fl-y, 0) * 0.5px));
  }
  /* his jaw and cheek, up and to the right of the match */
  .flame__face {
    width: calc(var(--fl-size, 60px) * 6);
    height: calc(var(--fl-size, 60px) * 5.4);
    margin: calc(var(--fl-size, 60px) * -5.2) 0 0 calc(var(--fl-size, 60px) * -0.6);
    background: radial-gradient(ellipse closest-side at 50% 50%, rgba(255, 176, 96, 0.2) 0%, rgba(255, 150, 70, 0.08) 50%, rgba(255, 140, 60, 0.02) 80%, rgba(255, 140, 60, 0) 100%);
    opacity: calc(0.35 + var(--fl-i, 0.9) * 0.75);
  }
  @keyframes flameIdle { 0%, 100% { opacity: 1; transform: scale(1); } 37% { opacity: 0.9; transform: scale(0.97, 1.03); } 68% { opacity: 0.96; transform: scale(1.02, 0.98); } }

  /* 和 — wa, harmony — behind his mark: gold, screened onto the dark so it
     glows rather than sits, rising slower than the page (18vh over the whole
     arrival) and settling from a little larger. */
  .arrive__kanji {
    position: absolute;
    left: 50%;
    top: -4vh;
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--kanji);
    font-size: clamp(14rem, 44vh, 30rem);
    line-height: 1;
    background: linear-gradient(170deg, #f2c275 10%, #b07932 90%);
    -webkit-background-clip: text;
    background-clip: text;
    -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;
    color: #daa24f;
    mix-blend-mode: screen;
    opacity: calc(var(--a-brand) * 0.3);
    transform: translate(-50%, calc((1 - var(--mp, 0)) * 18vh)) scale(calc(1.1 - var(--a-brand) * 0.1));
    pointer-events: none;
    user-select: none;
    will-change: transform, opacity;
  }
  /* The two columns either side of the mark, set vertically as the language
     is, the romaji beside them. The 和 rises as the page moves; these two
     settle down into place at different rates, so the three layers come
     apart — and, coming from above, never cross the words below them. */
  .arrive__vert {
    position: absolute;
    top: clamp(5.5rem, 13vh, 9rem);
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 0.45rem;
    writing-mode: vertical-rl;
    color: #f2c275;
    opacity: calc(var(--a-brand) * 0.82);
    pointer-events: none;
    user-select: none;
    will-change: transform, opacity;
  }
  .arrive__vert span {
    font-family: var(--kanji);
    font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 1.2rem + 1.6vw, 3rem);
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: 0.32em;
    text-shadow: 0 2px 24px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5);
  }
  .arrive__vert small {
    font-family: var(--font-avant);
    font-size: 0.6rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.3em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: rgba(252, 250, 248, 0.55);
  }
  .arrive__vert--l { left: var(--pad-x); transform: translateY(calc((1 - var(--mp, 0)) * -16vh)); }
  .arrive__vert--r { right: var(--pad-x); transform: translateY(calc((1 - var(--mp, 0)) * -6vh)); }
